  "notes": [
    "K3 (transfer gain = K2/K1) is the marquee linear-coupler spec and is stored dimensionless (unit 1); Vishay prints its unit column literally as 'K2/K1'. K1 (servo) and K2 (forward) gains are likewise bare ratios (unit 1).",
    "Transfer gain stability dK3/dTA is printed as +/-0.005 %/degC (typ) / +/-0.15 %/degC (max) and converted to ppm/degC by x1e4 (typ 50, max 1500).",
    "Completeness signals - printed, guaranteed specs with no key in the optocoupler dictionary, kept out of parameters rather than forced into a wrong key: (1) Common mode capacitance CCM = 1 pF (typ) at VF = 0 V, f = 1 MHz (page 3) - distinct from the input-output barrier capacitance CIO; (2) Phase response = -45 deg (typ) at 200 kHz, Vdet = -15 V (page 3). The output power dissipation (50 mW) is mapped to collector_power_dissipation (alias 'output power dissipation'), the only output-side dissipation key. (CMRR = 100 dB and the OUTPUT reverse voltage VR = 50 V, previously listed here, are now promoted to first-class parameters.)",
    "The OUTPUT power dissipation abs-max (50 mW) is carried under collector_power_dissipation; the IL300 output element is a PIN photodiode, not a phototransistor collector, but that key's aliases cover 'output/detector power dissipation'."
  ],
